<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Russian Civil War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a>–<a href="/years/1922">1922</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · <a href="/encyclopedia/wars">All wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Russian Civil War was fought from 1917 to 1922 between the Bolshevik <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> and a range of opponents, chiefly the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-movement">White movement</a>, with nationalist forces and foreign interventions also involved. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolsheviks">Bolsheviks</a> defeated the White armies of Kolchak, Denikin, Yudenich and Wrangel and in 1922 founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>; millions died in the fighting, terror, famine and epidemics.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war.jpg" alt="Russian Civil War" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yanachka · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CWRArticleImage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Background</h2><p>The war began with the overthrow of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-provisional-government">Russian Provisional Government</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a>. The monarchy had ended with the abdication of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/february-revolution">February Revolution</a> of 1917, after which a coalition of centrist parties governed beside soviets of workers, soldiers and peasants. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolsheviks">Bolsheviks</a> directed the Red Guard to seize <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a> and began taking cities across the former empire. In January 1918 they dissolved the Constituent Assembly, in which the anti-Bolshevik Right Socialist-Revolutionaries had won the most seats. The conflict became a full-scale civil war in May and June 1918.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Course of events</h2><p>The two largest combatants were the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a>, fighting for a Bolshevik-led socialist state under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-lenin">Vladimir Lenin</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-movement">White movement</a>, led mainly by right-leaning officers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>. Ukrainian anarchists and Left Socialist-Revolutionaries also fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolsheviks">Bolsheviks</a>. Thirteen foreign states intervened against the Red Army, chiefly the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>, who aimed first to restore the Eastern Front of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. In May 1918 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovak-legion">Czechoslovak Legion</a> revolted in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>, and the former tsar and his family were murdered on 17 July. After an uprising of the Left Socialist-Revolutionaries in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> that July, executions grew more frequent and the Red Terror began.</p><p>In 1919 the Whites attacked from the east in March, the south in July and the west in October, and each advance was checked by a Red counteroffensive. Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-kolchak">Alexander Kolchak</a>'s army disintegrated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> forced evacuations from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/novorossiysk">Novorossiysk</a> in March and from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a> in November 1920, and fighting was then sporadic until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladivostok">Vladivostok</a> was captured in October 1922.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Aftermath and significance</h2><p>Estimates put the casualties at 7 to 12 million, mostly civilians. A famine caused between 3 and 10 million deaths, and by 1921 heavy industry produced only 20 percent of its 1913 output. One to two million people fled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, many with General Wrangel, among them a large share of the educated and skilled population.</p><p>Many non-Russian peoples used the disorder to press for independence. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, Latvia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> repelled Soviet invasions, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> were occupied by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a>. The Basmachi resistance in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> was not dismantled until 1934. With the failure of revolutions elsewhere, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolsheviks">Bolsheviks</a> moved from world revolution to socialism in one country, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Russian Civil War” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…by Tomáš Garrigue Masaryk, Edvard Beneš and the Slovak astronomer and general Milan Rastislav Štefánik, whose Czechoslovak National Council in Paris won Allied recognition in 1918, helped by the fame of the Czechoslovak Legion, which had fought its way along the Trans-Siberian Railway during the <b>Russian Civil War</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Anarchists have taken part in several revolutions, most notably the Paris Commune, the <b>Russian Civil War</b> and the Spanish Civil War.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/anarchism">Anarchism · In Power</a></li><li><blockquote>In the <b>Russian Civil War</b> it served as an unofficial anthem of Admiral Kolchak's White Army, while its earliest known performance by communist troops dates from 1918.</blockquote><a href="/songs/farewell-of-slavianka">Farewell of Slavianka</a></li><li><blockquote>It was written in 1920, during the <b>Russian Civil War</b>, as a combat anthem for the Red Army.</blockquote><a href="/songs/the-red-army-is-the-strongest">The Red Army Is the Strongest</a></li><li><blockquote>By the end of the <b>Russian Civil War</b> in 1922 it had at least 200,000 personnel.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/december-20">20 December in history</a></li><li><blockquote>During the <b>Russian Civil War</b> the Ural Cossacks fought the Bolsheviks, and the host was destroyed in 1920.</blockquote><a href="/state/ural-cossack-host">Ural Cossack Host</a></li></ul></section>
